{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["For I am heavy of mouth and uncircumcised of lips — I am not fluent in the Egyptian tongue in precise articulation, for in my youth I fled from there, and now I am eighty years old. So too we find in Ezekiel that one who is not fluent in the royal tongue is so called, as it is written: ״ויאמר אלי בן אדם לך בא אל בית ישראל ודברת דברי אליהם. כי לא אל עם עמקי שפה וכבדי לשון אתה שלוח אל בית ישראל לא אל עמים עמקי שפה וכבדי לשון אשר לא תשמע דבריהם וגו׳״. And is it possible that a prophet whom HaShem knew face to face and who received the Torah directly from His hand would stammer in his speech?! And this matter is not found in the words of the Tannaim and Amoraim, and one should not rely on external books."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "Rashbam quotes Ezekiel 3:4–6 with slight paraphrase; the Hebrew lemma is left unaddressed as is his custom for supporting quotations."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:40:20.763415417Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}